<div class="eco" id="top">
  <h1>💰 The PAT Economy</h1>
  <p class="sub">Everything you can do with PAT: earn it, gamble it, bet it, lend it, stake it, or steal it.
    Most of it runs through Pepe in the Camfrog rooms, and a lot of it works right here on the site too.</p>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
    <div class="lbl">JUMP TO</div>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#pat">🪙 What is PAT</a></li>
      <li><a href="#flow">🏛️ Where PAT goes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#casino">🎰 Casino</a></li>
      <li><a href="#betting">🤝 Wagers &amp; pools</a></li>
      <li><a href="#markets">📈 Markets</a></li>
      <li><a href="#judge">🤖 AI judge</a></li>
      <li><a href="#bounties">🎯 Bounties</a></li>
      <li><a href="#loans">🏦 Loans</a></li>
      <li><a href="#stash">🔐 Stashes &amp; staking</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gtf">🔫 Grand Theft Frog</a></li>
      <li><a href="#polls">🗳️ Polls</a></li>
      <li><a href="#web">🌐 On the website</a></li>
      <li><a href="#fees">🧾 Fees</a></li>
      <li><a href="#links">🔗 Links</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- 1. PAT -->
  <section id="pat">
    <div class="kicker">THE BASICS</div>
    <h2>🪙 What PAT is</h2>
    <p class="lead">PAT (Public Access Token) is the points currency of PATV. It's one balance shared by the website, the
      Camfrog rooms and Discord, so PAT you win from Pepe in a room is the same PAT you spend on the site.
      It isn't crypto and it isn't real money, but you can spend it on real prizes in the <a href="/shop">shop</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>💬 Hang out</h3>
        <p>Chatting in a room enters you in Pepe's automatic raffles, and whoever spends the most time on mic each hour
          gets a top-mic reward. Chat messages and mic time also earn XP.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!xp</code> · <code>!level</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>⬆️ Level up</h3>
        <p>1 XP per chat message, 1 XP per second on mic. Every new level pays a PAT reward that grows with your level,
          plus a stat point every 10 levels for your heist character.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏅 Achievements</h3>
        <p>100 achievements for chatting, mic time, games, heists and more. Each one is a pixel badge on your profile,
          plus XP and a PAT bonus.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!achievements</code> · <a href="/achievements">/achievements</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎲 Play</h3>
        <p>Spin the wheel, win at the tables, win trivia, crack a vault, collect on a good bet. Getting tipped counts too:
          anyone can send you PAT with <code>!tip</code>.</p>
        <div class="cmd">Broke? <code>!beg</code> for a small handout (only when you're nearly out).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card wide">
        <h3>👛 Your wallet and history</h3>
        <p>Your balance shows on your profile. <a href="/history">/history</a> lists every PAT transaction on your account
          (tips, wins, bets, bonuses), and <code>!history</code> shows your last five in chat.
          The <a href="/rankings">leaderboard</a> shows the top balances and the <b>total PAT supply</b>: every PAT that
          exists, in wallets, vaults, escrow and stashes. Link your Camfrog name on your profile (then type
          <code>!verify</code> with the code) so your room PAT and site PAT are one balance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Flow -->
  <section id="flow">
    <div class="kicker">MONEY FLOW</div>
    <h2>🏛️ Where PAT goes</h2>
    <p class="lead">When you pay for something (a spin, a ticket, a fee, a paid command) that PAT doesn't vanish.
      <b>PAT is never burned.</b> It moves into one of the pools below, and those pools pay it back out as prizes,
      heist loot and rewards.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏛️ The Federal Reserve</h3>
        <p>The big central vault. It collects most non-gambling spending, pays level-up and achievement rewards,
          seeds the prediction markets, lends PAT, and is the target of the legendary bank heist.
          <code>!reserve</code> shows its balance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎰 The casino jackpot</h3>
        <p>The casino's bank. Wheel spins, casino rake, losing bets and lotto tickets go in; it pays the wheel,
          blackjack wins, the lottery and the casino heist. <code>!jackpot</code> (or <code>!vault</code>) shows what's in it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🧭 The routing table</h3>
        <p>Every fee in the game has a row in one table that says where it goes: the Reserve, the casino jackpot,
          a gang's turf business, or stakers. Each fee can be split, and whatever isn't routed somewhere else lands
          in the Reserve. The admins tune the splits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🔒 Escrow</h3>
        <p>When you stake PAT on something that takes days (a wager, a market, a loan, a bounty, a bingo card) it leaves
          your wallet straight away and is held in escrow. Every step is recorded, so if Pepe restarts mid-game your
          PAT is either paid out or refunded: never lost, never paid twice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>You spend PAT</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>Reserve · Jackpot · Turf · Stakers</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>Prizes · Loot · Rewards</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>Your wallet</span>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Casino -->
  <section id="casino">
    <div class="kicker">GAMES OF CHANCE</div>
    <h2>🎰 The casino</h2>
    <p class="lead">Pepe runs the tables in the Camfrog rooms and shows the action on stream. Each game runs in one room;
      Pepe tells you where to head if you type a command somewhere else.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎡 Wheel of Misfortune</h3>
        <p>5,000 PAT a spin, on the site or in chat. Where it stops is what you win. The thin gold slice is the
          jackpot: it hits about 1 in 3,000 spins and pays a share of the casino jackpot (up to 5M).</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!spin</code> · or the wheel on your profile</div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> every spin into the casino jackpot, which pays the prizes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🂡 Blackjack</h3>
        <p>Pepe deals from a 6-deck shoe, shuffled fresh and provably fair every round. Blackjack pays 3:2, dealer hits
          soft 17. Double, split (up to 4 hands), insurance. Bets 100 to 10,000 PAT, up to 6 players.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!bj start</code> · <code>!bet 500</code> · <code>!hit</code> / <code>!stand</code> · <code>!autobet</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> the house pays winners; half of every losing bet feeds the jackpot.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🂠 Texas Hold'em</h3>
        <p>No-limit cash game in chat. Chips are PAT 1:1: buy in to sit (20 to 200 big blinds), cash out any time.
          Your hole cards come by private message. Up to 9 players. Can't run alongside a blackjack table.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!holdem start 25/50</code> · <code>!sit 5000</code> · <code>!call</code> · <code>!raise 600</code> · <code>!stand</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> pots go to the winners, minus a small rake set by the admins.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎟️ PAT Lottery</h3>
        <p>Powerball-style, drawn every Sunday at 9pm ET, ball by ball on stream. Pick 4 numbers from 1–30 plus a Pepe Ball
          from 1–10, or let Pepe pick. 1,000 PAT a ticket, no limit. All 4 + Pepe Ball wins the jackpot
          (1 in 274,050); smaller prizes from 1k to 500k, and about 1 in 6 tickets wins something.
          Results are on <a href="/lotto">/lotto</a>.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!lotto 3 7 12 25 pb 4</code> · <code>!lotto quick 20</code> · <code>!lotto odds</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> tickets go into the casino jackpot, which <i>is</i> the lotto jackpot. It grows all week, unless a crew robs the casino first.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🔢 Bingo</h3>
        <p>75-ball bingo on the stream overlay. Cards are 2,500 PAT (up to 4), sent by PM. Type <code>!bingo</code> the moment
          you have a line; Pepe checks it for you. First line wins 30% of the prize pool, first full card wins the rest.
          A wrong call costs 1,000 PAT and a 60s sit-out.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!bingo start</code> · <code>!bingo buy 3</code> · <code>!bingo</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> 10% of card sales to the casino, the rest is the prize pool. Unclaimed prizes roll into the next game.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🧠 Trivia</h3>
        <p>Everyone pays the buy-in (default 1,000 PAT) into one pot and the winner takes it all. Pick a topic if you like.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!trivia 5000 movies</code> · <code>!join</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> player to player, winner takes the pot.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>💲 Showdown</h3>
        <p>Price-is-Right style: guess Pepe's secret number (1–10,000). 10,000 PAT buy-in, closest without going over takes the
          pot, and nailing it exactly pays a bonus.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!showdown</code> · <code>!guess 4200</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> the pot is just the buy-ins, back to the players.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>⚔️ Duels, brawls &amp; the Arena</h3>
        <p>Dice duels (100 to 50,000 PAT), 1v1 brawls using your heist character's stats, and the Arena: a battle royale where
          the last fighter standing takes the pot.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!duel @bob 5000</code> · <code>!brawl @bob 10k</code> · <code>!arena 5000</code> · <code>!accept</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> winner takes the pot; brawls and the Arena send a small cut to the jackpot.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎨 Pictionary</h3>
        <p>Pepe draws live on stream, you guess in chat. Free to play; the first right guess each round wins PAT.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!pictionary 5 animals</code></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Betting between people -->
  <section id="betting">
    <div class="kicker">PLAYER VS PLAYER</div>
    <h2>🤝 Wagers &amp; betting pools</h2>
    <p class="lead">Bet on anything that happens, in the room or out in the world. Somebody you both trust is the judge
      and calls the result. Stakes sit in escrow until then. Everything shows on <a href="/wagers">/wagers</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🤝 1-on-1 wagers</h3>
        <p>Challenge one person. Your stake is held right away; they have 10 minutes to accept and match it.
          The judge (anyone but the two of you) picks the winner, or voids it to refund both. Min 1,000 PAT.
          If the judge doesn't settle by the deadline (default 7 days, max 30), both get their PAT back.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!wager @bob 10k Lakers win tonight judge @carol by 2d</code><br><code>!accept</code> · <code>!wager settle W12 @bob</code> · <code>!wager list</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> winner takes the pot minus a 5% fee.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>👥 Betting pools <span class="new">NEW</span></h3>
        <p>A bet the whole room can get in on. Make a question (yes/no, or your own options), name a judge, and everyone
          backs the side they like with as much as they want. When the judge calls it, the winners split the losing side's
          pool in proportion to what they put in, so a correct bet never comes back smaller than it went in.
          This is the classic racetrack (parimutuel) model.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!pool new Will it rain Friday? judge @carol closes 2d</code><br><code>!pool new Who wins? judge @carol options a/b/c</code><br><code>!pool M5 yes 5k</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> winners get their stake back plus their share of the losing pool, minus 5% of the losing side (set by the admins). If nobody backed the winner, or it's voided, everyone is refunded.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note">Pools vs markets: in a pool your odds are only fixed when betting closes and you can't get out early.
      In a <a href="#markets">prediction market</a> you buy at today's price and can sell any time.</div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. Markets -->
  <section id="markets">
    <div class="kicker">TRADE THE ODDS</div>
    <h2>📈 Prediction markets</h2>
    <p class="lead">Polymarket-style share trading. Each answer has a price between 0 and 1 PAT, and that price is the
      crowd's odds: 0.70 means "about 70% likely". Every share of the winning answer pays out 1 PAT, losing shares pay 0.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>📊 How it works</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Buying pushes an answer's price up, selling pushes it down.</li>
          <li>Sell any time while trading's open: lock in a profit or cut a loss before the result.</li>
          <li>Yes/no by default, or 2–6 answers. Trading closes at the set time (default 1 day, max 30).</li>
          <li>The judge can't trade. A void refunds what holders paid.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>⌨️ Commands</h3>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!market new Will Sam come back this week? judge @carol closes 2d</code><br>
          <code>!market M3 yes 5k</code> (spend 5k, min 500)<br>
          <code>!market sell M3 yes all</code><br>
          <code>!market mine</code> · <code>!market list</code></div>
        <p>Your positions on <a href="/markets">/markets</a> show your entry price, today's price and your profit or loss, with a price chart.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏛️ Who pays the winners?</h3>
        <p>An automated market maker (LMSR, the maths behind many prediction sites) is always there to trade with you.
          The Federal Reserve seeds each market's liquidity and the pot can always cover every winning share.
          What's left over afterwards goes back to the Reserve.</p>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> 2% fee on every buy and sell, routed by the routing table.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. AI judge -->
  <section id="judge">
    <div class="kicker">EXPERIMENTAL</div>
    <h2>🤖 Pepe as judge <span class="new exp">NEW · EXPERIMENTAL</span></h2>
    <p class="lead">No neutral human around? A market, pool or wager can name Pepe himself as the judge.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>1. Name him</h3>
        <p>Use <code>judge @pepe</code> when you create it. Works best for questions with a clear, checkable answer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>2. He proposes</h3>
        <p>When it's time, Pepe proposes a result and posts his reasoning so everyone can see why.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>3. Dispute window</h3>
        <p>Players then get a dispute window (default 1 hour) to object if they think he got it wrong:</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!market dispute M3 why</code> · <code>!wager dispute W3 why</code> · ask him early: <code>!market ai M3</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>4. Pay out or escalate</h3>
        <p>Enough disputes and it goes to an admin to decide. Otherwise it pays out automatically when the window closes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note warn">This is new. Pepe can be wrong, so read his reasoning and use the dispute window if you disagree.</div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. Bounties -->
  <section id="bounties">
    <div class="kicker">GET STUFF DONE</div>
    <h2>🎯 Bounties</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p>Put PAT up for someone to do something. Others can chip in to grow the pot. Hunters claim it ("I did it"),
          and the poster pays whoever pulled it off; several hunters split it evenly. You can't claim your own bounty.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!bounty kick plantbaked 1000 by 2d</code> · <code>!bounty add BT3 500</code><br><code>!bounty claim BT3</code> · <code>!bounty resolve BT3 @hunter</code> · <code>!bounties</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> held in escrow; the hunters get the pot minus a 5% fee. Cancelled or expired (default 7 days)? Everyone who put money in is refunded.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🌐 On the site</h3>
        <p>See every bounty on <a href="/bounties">/bounties</a>, chip in, claim one with a note, and (if you posted it)
          pay the hunters or cancel.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8. Loans -->
  <section id="loans">
    <div class="kicker">CREDIT</div>
    <h2>🏦 Loans</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🤝 Person to person</h3>
        <p>Lend PAT with interest (a flat rate for the term, max 50%). The amount is held from you right away; they have
          10 minutes to accept. Borrowers can repay early, in part or in full.</p>
        <p>When it's due, Pepe collects automatically: whatever they have, then the rest as PAT comes in. Anything still
          owed grows 2% a day (capped at +50% of the loan) and the borrower carries a public <b>LATE</b> mark until square.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!loan @bob 50k 10% 7d</code> · <code>!loan repay L5</code> · <code>!loan check @bob</code> · <code>!loans</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> the lender always gets the full amount back; 10% of the interest and penalties goes to the Reserve.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏛️ Federal Reserve loans <span class="new">NEW</span></h3>
        <p>Borrow straight from the Reserve at the Reserve's rate. Within your limit it's approved instantly; your limit grows
          with your level and a clean repayment record. Want more? Ask the admins, who can also grant loans themselves.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!loan reserve 50k 7d</code> · <code>!loan request 200k 14d why</code> (bigger amounts) · <code>!loan reserve</code> shows your limit</div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> principal and interest go back to the Reserve. Unpaid loans are collected automatically,
          and a late borrower is marked LATE and can't borrow again until they're square.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9. Stashes & staking -->
  <section id="stash">
    <div class="kicker">SAVE &amp; EARN</div>
    <h2>🔐 Stashes &amp; staking</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🔐 Stashes</h3>
        <p>Personal vaults. Park PAT outside your wallet and share it with accounts you trust: anyone you grant can
          deposit and withdraw. Up to 3 stashes, 10 members each. Closing one pays what's left to the owner.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!stash create savings</code> · <code>!stash deposit savings 50k</code><br><code>!stash grant savings @myalt</code> · <code>!stash withdraw savings 10k</code> · <code>!stash list</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>📈 Staking <span class="new">NEW</span></h3>
        <p>Stake PAT in a stash to earn a share of the game fees that are routed to stakers. Payouts are daily, split by how much
          you staked and for how long, and they auto-compound (your earnings are staked too).</p>
        <p>The yield floats inside a target range the admins set: the share of fees sent to stakers is turned up or down to keep it
          in range, and the Reserve can top it up if it drops below.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!stash stake savings 100k</code> · <code>!stash unstake savings all</code> · <code>!stash yield</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>👛 Your wallet page</h3>
        <p>See your stashes, staked PAT and loans in one place on <a href="/wallet">/wallet</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 10. GTF -->
  <section id="gtf">
    <div class="kicker">CRIME PAYS</div>
    <h2>🔫 Grand Theft Frog</h2>
    <p class="lead">The crime side of PATV. Roll a character with <code>!sheet</code> and go to work. Full guide on <a href="/gtf">/gtf</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🥷 Heists</h3>
        <p>Crew up and survive rounds of dice rolls to bank loot; bail out or go for the vault door. The store is always open;
          the casino job robs the casino jackpot and the bank job cracks the Federal Reserve.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!heist</code> · <code>!join</code> · <code>!bail</code> · <code>!shop</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> heists pay out of the vaults, like a dividend. A failed vault door leaves the loot in the vault. PAT is never burned.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🗺️ Turf Wars</h3>
        <p>Gangs fight over the districts on this season's map (the map changes every season). Each district runs a business
          that earns its owner PAT every day. Claim, raid, defend, and climb the season score.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!turf</code> · <code>!claim</code> · <code>!raid</code></div>
        <div class="goes"><b>PAT goes:</b> some fees route to the gang that owns the matching turf business.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎩 Gangs</h3>
        <p>A gang shares a treasury, wages and heat. Take turf together, defend it together, split what it earns.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!gang create [TAG] name</code> · <code>!gang invite @user</code></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 11. Polls -->
  <section id="polls">
    <div class="kicker">HAVE YOUR SAY</div>
    <h2>🗳️ Polls</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p>Free, no PAT involved. One vote per person, in the room or on the site. Every poll gets a live results page;
          see them all on <a href="/polls">/polls</a>.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!poll Best pizza? pepperoni, margherita, pineapple</code> · type the number to vote · <code>!results</code></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 12. Website -->
  <section id="web">
    <div class="kicker">NO CAMFROG NEEDED</div>
    <h2>🌐 Doing it all from the website</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p>Once your Camfrog name is linked to your PATV account (start the link on your profile, then type
          <code>!verify</code> with the code in a room), you can do most of this right here:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>create and trade <a href="/markets">markets</a>, join <a href="/wagers">pools and wagers</a></li>
          <li>post, fund and claim <a href="/bounties">bounties</a></li>
          <li>vote in and start <a href="/polls">polls</a></li>
          <li>buy <a href="/lotto">lotto</a> tickets</li>
          <li>manage your stashes and loans on <a href="/wallet">/wallet</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>It's the same balance and the same rules as in the room; Pepe places your orders through the normal checks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fees -->
  <section id="fees">
    <div class="kicker">AT A GLANCE</div>
    <h2>🧾 Fees</h2>
    <p class="lead">Fees aren't burned: each one is routed to the Reserve, the casino jackpot, turf businesses or stakers.
      <span class="cfg">⚙ = set by the admins, can change.</span></p>
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>WHAT</th><th>FEE</th><th>NOTES</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Wheel spin</td><td class="n">5,000 / spin</td><td>All into the casino jackpot, which pays the prizes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Blackjack</td><td class="n">½ of losing bets</td><td>To the casino jackpot; winners paid by the house</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hold'em</td><td class="n">small rake <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Taken from pots</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Lotto ticket</td><td class="n">1,000 / ticket</td><td>Whole ticket into the casino jackpot (the lotto jackpot)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bingo</td><td class="n">10% of card sales</td><td>To the casino; the rest is the prize pool</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1-on-1 wager</td><td class="n">5% of the pot</td><td>Only when someone wins; voids are free</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Betting pool</td><td class="n">5% of losing side <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Winners never get back less than they bet</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Prediction market</td><td class="n">2% per trade</td><td>On every buy and sell</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bounty</td><td class="n">5% of payout</td><td>Refunds on cancel or expiry are free</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Player loan</td><td class="n">10% of interest</td><td>To the Reserve; principal never taxed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Late loan</td><td class="n">+2% / day</td><td>On what's still owed, capped at +50% of the loan</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Brawl / Arena</td><td class="n">small cut <span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>To the casino jackpot</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Fee splits</td><td class="n"><span class="cfg">⚙</span></td><td>Where each fee goes is set in the routing table</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

